 "result": "The round-trip is done by a tag-based JSON serializer.\n\n**Serializer** — `src/tessel/json/tag.py`\n- `TypedCookieSerializer` (line 219) walks the data and, on dump, converts each non-JSON type into a one-key tagged dict. On load it reverses the conversion.\n- `TypeMarker` (line 60) is the base class for the per-type tags. Each tag checks whether a value is its type, converts it to JSON-safe form, and converts it back.\n\n**Tags**\n- `TagTuple` (line 133): tuples\n- `TagBytes` (line 159): bytes, stored base64-encoded\n- `TagDateTime` (line 205): datetimes, stored as an HTTP date string\n- `TagDict` (line 93): dicts that already look like a tag, so they aren't misread on load\n- `PassDict` (line 119) and `PassList` (line 147): recurse into plain containers\n- `TagMarkup` (line 173) and `TagUUID` (line 191): Markup and UUID values\n\n**Session wiring** — `src/tessel/sessions.py`\n- `session_json_serializer = TypedCookieSerializer()` (line 273) is the module-level instance.\n- `SignedCookieSessionInterface` (line 284) uses it as `serializer` (line 300), so it handles the signed cookie payload.\n- `SignedCookieSession` (line 57) is the session object itself. The interface serializes and deserializes it on save and open.",
